      <div class="section-heading reveal">
        <p class="section-index">Export & Assembly</p>
        <h2>Export Delivery and Site Assembly Considerations</h2>
        <p>ZhongSai truss structures are designed and packed for export delivery, with careful consideration of transport segmentation, container loading and site assembly requirements.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="export-grid">
        <div class="export-item reveal">
          <h4>Component Marking</h4>
          <p>Unique truss and member identification system matching assembly drawings, including piece marks, orientation marks and connection references for accurate site assembly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="export-item reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <h4>Packing Organization</h4>
          <p>Truss members packed by assembly sequence and connection groups, with protective packaging for finished surfaces and threaded components. Detailed packing lists included.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="export-item reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <h4>Container Loading</h4>
          <p>Optimized container loading plan maximizing space utilization while protecting truss members. Loading diagrams and container packing records provided per project requirements.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="export-item reveal">
          <h4>Oversized Member Segmentation</h4>
          <p>Long truss members segmented for container and road transport limits, with designed splice connections for site assembly. Segmentation optimized to minimize site connections.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="export-item reveal reveal-delay-1">
          <h4>Bolted Site Connections</h4>
          <p>Bolted connections designed for site assembly with pre-drilled holes, high-strength bolts and clear assembly instructions. Connection accessibility considered during detailing.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="export-item reveal reveal-delay-2">
          <h4>Installation Sequence</h4>
          <p>Site erection sequence considerations including temporary support requirements, connection accessibility, lifting points and safety considerations for truss installation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">
        <a href="/en/export-delivery/" class="btn btn-outline">View Export & Delivery →</a>
